meta {
  name: Simulate a member leaving
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{groupAdmin}}/roster
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "key": "{{groupKey}}",
    "members": ["{{memberName}}"]
  }
}

tests {
  test("closes what the member who is no longer named was holding", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.members).to.not.include(bru.getEnvVar("secondMember"));
    expect(res.body.failed || []).to.be.an("array").that.is.empty;
  });
}

docs {
  # Simulate a member leaving

  The same request as `State the roster` with one member gone, which is the whole of what leaving is.

  Run it while `{{secondMember}}` has a stream open, and their connections come back under `kicked` and their player stops.
  Anything `{{memberName}}` holds is untouched, `kept` counting it.

  A member who left still holds a token until it expires, so opening another stream works until then.
  The relay reports that read as it starts and the group service runs this again (`Reconcile`, `deploy/reconcile-on-read.sh`), which is what closes the second attempt.
  Keeping them out for good is the other half, and it belongs to whatever hands out tokens: a member who left is one it stops issuing to.
}
